-- title:
--   The heat semigroup solves the heat equation
-- statement:
--   Let $E=\mathbb R^\iota$ be a finite-dimensional Euclidean space with standard Gaussian measure $\gamma$, and for a function $F$ on $E$ let $P_tF(x)=\int F(x+\sqrt t\,z)\,d\gamma(z)$ be the Gaussian heat semigroup. Let $F:E\to\mathbb R$ be bounded with gradient $g$ and Hessian $K$, where $g$ is bounded and $K$ is continuous and bounded. Then for $t>0$,
--   $$
--   \frac{\partial}{\partial t}P_tF(x)=\frac12\sum_i\bigl\langle(P_tK)(x)\,e_i,e_i\bigr\rangle=\frac12\,\Delta P_tF(x).
--   $$
--
--   So $P_t$ is the semigroup generated by half the Laplacian.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Probability/GaussianPropeller/HeatConvolution.lean#L170-L206

